{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "0DBC", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Sch_{ph}$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$S$", "MATH_0005": "$(\\Sch/S)_{ph}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Sch_{ph}/S$", "MATH_0007": "$S$", "MATH_0008": "$(\\textit{Aff}/S)_{ph}$", "MATH_0009": "$(\\Sch/S)_{ph}$", "MATH_0010": "$U/S$", "MATH_0011": "$(\\textit{Aff}/S)_{ph}$", "MATH_0012": "$\\{U_i \\to U\\}$", "MATH_0013": "$(\\Sch/S)_{ph}$", "MATH_0014": "$U_i$", "MATH_0015": "$U$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-section-localize}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-big-small-ph}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9377300f1f8b6a640c52c62a44a2f9d796df6ada6932b76f656b2723ddbc7871", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:937bac4b0607fbff8be2cafdcee6f96d00083ea17e8b20d57fac2a7665fa390b", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be a big ph site containing <MATH_0003>.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> The <TEXTITOPEN_0001>big ph site of <MATH_0004><TEXTITCLOSE_0001>, denoted\n<MATH_0005>, is the site <MATH_0006>\nintroduced in Sites, Section <REF_0001>.\n<STRUCT_0003> The <TEXTITOPEN_0002>big affine ph site of <MATH_0007><TEXTITCLOSE_0002>, denoted\n<MATH_0008>, is the full subcategory of\n<MATH_0009> whose objects are affine <MATH_0010>.\nA covering of <MATH_0011> is any finite covering\n<MATH_0012> of <MATH_0013> with <MATH_0014> and <MATH_0015> affine.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:64d721cd7d53396727f895a4f10decba25549f5c4857163aa86f05533ae2c16b", "unit_id": "tag:0DBL:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0DBC", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(\\textit{Aff}/S)_{ph}$", "MATH_0002": "$(\\textit{Aff}/S)_{ph}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\{U_i \\to U\\}$", "MATH_0004": "$(\\Sch/S)_{ph}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-definition-site}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c9767da38593ef8792af6d21943a5e697efb312ab0f64b712db0569e8b6c6110", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7981249a8ec6bc4d2bca519cf53175279a2263bc734fedc8adee50c30eaf841b", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nObserve that the coverings in <MATH_0001> are <TEXTITOPEN_0001>not<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\ngiven by standard ph coverings. The reason is simply that this would\nfail the second axiom of Sites, Definition <REF_0001>.\nRather, the coverings in <MATH_0002> are those finite families\n<MATH_0003> of finite type morphisms between affine objects\nof <MATH_0004> which can be refined by a standard ph covering.\nWe explicitly state and prove that the big affine ph site is a site.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5f451edcd5c2194926abd42eac5fc9d3a6007d838e7efd223821e8b3ecc1e134", "unit_id": "tag:0DBC:prose-0006"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0DBC", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Sch_{ph}$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$(\\textit{Aff}/S)_{ph}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-verify-site-ph}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:6f6befa271e4715099a745d3ae712c08523e2e5e0ea9128cad3fa3a53f21cc08", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5bedbd794391cad9972576539af3cc16b5fa78cc56e393730ef2260785068456", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be a big ph\nsite containing <MATH_0003>. Then <MATH_0004> is a site.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d85a995fe2f3f079b51d50a9c9477ac225f10af07e534803163fda2483c53e68", "unit_id": "tag:0DBM:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0DBC", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\{U_i \\to U\\}$", "MATH_0002": "$U$", "MATH_0003": "$U_i$", "MATH_0004": "$\\{T_i \\to T\\}_{i\\in I}$", "MATH_0005": "$T_i, T$", "MATH_0006": "$i$", "MATH_0007": "$\\{T_{ij} \\to T_i\\}_{j\\in J_i}$", "MATH_0008": "$T_{ij}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\{T_{ij} \\to T\\}_{i \\in I, j\\in J_i}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\bigcup_{i\\in I} J_i$", "MATH_0011": "$T_{ij}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-verify-site-etale}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{sites-definition-site}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-ph}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e54dfcb8b2d54564883b47133626ffc74844207bd3d50539f27ffb1821794463", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4a6171d9f1b8270c79ee4096d3f31edd235b823ecd107055c934e12187716381", "source_text": "Reasoning as in the proof of Lemma <REF_0001>\nit suffices to show that the collection of finite ph coverings\n<MATH_0001> with <MATH_0002>, <MATH_0003> affine satisfies properties\n(1), (2) and (3) of\nSites, Definition <REF_0002>.\nThis is clear since for example, given a finite ph covering\n<MATH_0004> with <MATH_0005> affine, and for each\n<MATH_0006> a finite ph covering <MATH_0007> with <MATH_0008>\naffine , then <MATH_0009> is a ph covering\n(Lemma <REF_0003>), <MATH_0010> is finite and\neach <MATH_0011> is affine.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:12b22b0e46b755d1205c04c9a8d6c313964d7af1dda2cba30dbf615cba958457", "unit_id": "tag:0DBM:proof"}
